                <pb facs="0749" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg645"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Salt Funds/96: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-30T18:00:00+08:00">March 30, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 30—8:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>391. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 30, 2 p.m. Supplementing my March 29, midnight,<anchor n="36"
                                xml:id="d688-f1"/> Japanese press reports that new government
                            announced on the 28th that the Salt Administration is hereafter
                            independent of Nanking and that all of its administrative functions will
                            be taken over by Changchun; that foreign obligations secured by the Salt
                            Gabelle will not be repudiated and claims entered by the creditor powers
                            will be considered; and that employees willing to sever connections with
                            the Chinese Government will be retained.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
